:4734   :ABORD       "10"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "10"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Near Centerville";
        :DATE        "1940-11-04"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "04:42";
        :OPERATOR    "United Air Lines";
        :REGION      "Utah";
        :ROUTE       "Oakland - Salt Lake City";
        :SUMMARY     "The aircraft crashed into Bountiful Peak in the Wasatch Mountains, during a snowstorm, 3 nm NE of Centerville. The failure of the communications operators at Tintic, Plymouth, and Salt Lake City, Utah, whose duty it was to monitor the range, to detect its malfunctioning and immediately notify those concerned and the failure of the pilot to follow to the fullest extent established radio range technique in accordance with the requirements of the procedure established by United and approved by the Civil Aeronautics Administration.";
        :TYPE        "Douglas DC-3".

:1592   :ABORD       "26"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "26"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Near La Bonita";
        :DATE        "2002-01-17"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "11:00";
        :OPERATOR    "Petroproducción";
        :REGION      "Ecuador";
        :ROUTE       "Quito - Lago Agrio";
        :SUMMARY     "The plane crashed into del cerro El Tigre mountain in the jungles of the Amazon at an elevation of 14,700 ft.  The 35 minute flight was transporting oil workers to a remote oil field.";
        :TYPE        "Fairchild FH-227E".

:3830   :ABORD       "127"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "0"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Bacolod";
        :DATE        "1998-03-22"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "3"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "19:42";
        :OPERATOR    "Philippine Air Lines";
        :REGION      "Philippines";
        :ROUTE       "Manila - Bacolod";
        :SUMMARY     "The aircraft overran the 6,888 ft. runway, went through a concrete perimeter fence, crossed a small river and hit a karaoke house before stopping near a market. The plane was (legally) released from Manila with the No. 1 reverser deactivated. The plane landed mid-runway and the crew incorrectly used the No. 2 reverser to try and stop the plane causing it to veer to the right. The No. 2 engine was then to set to forward thrust steering the plane back on the runway.  A go-around was attempted but it was too late and the aircraft overran the runway.";
        :TYPE        "Airbus A.320-214".

:2686   :ABORD       "72"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "64"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Near Tokyo";
        :DATE        "1966-03-04"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "20:15";
        :OPERATOR    "Canadian PacifiAir Lines";
        :REGION      "Japan";
        :ROUTE       "Hong Kong - Tokyo";
        :SUMMARY     "The aircraft struck the approach lights and a sea wall during a landing attempt. The pilot initiated a steep rate of descent with the intention of executing a final approach at a lower altitude. Poor visibility due to illusive fog conditions misled the pilot and affected his judgement.";
        :TYPE        "McDonnell Douglas DC-8-43".

:4924   :ABORD       "25"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "7"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Selleck";
        :DATE        "1953-04-14"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "02:22";
        :OPERATOR    "Miami Airlines";
        :REGION      "Washington";
        :ROUTE       "Spokane - Ellenburgh";
        :SUMMARY     "The aircraft crashed into Cedar Mountain following double engine failure. The progressive failure of both engines, due to the lack of compliance with proper maintenance standards. Spark plugs in both engines had been operated beyond their normal maintenance inspection period and exhibited evidence of a condition conducive to detonation and preignition. There was evidence that detonation and preignition took place in both engines and that  they ultimately failed as a result of master rod bearing failures.";
        :TYPE        "Douglas DC-3 (C-47-DL)".

:1782   :ABORD       "9"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "9"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Bua";
        :DATE        "1979-07-12"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :OPERATOR    "Fiji Air Services";
        :REGION      "Fiji";
        :ROUTE       "Suva-Nausori - Bua-Dama";
        :SUMMARY     "Crashed into a rain forest. Pilot-in-command continuing the flight into conditions where he lost visual reference with the ground which resulted in the aircraft colliding with terrain.";
        :TYPE        "Britten Norman BN-2A Trislander".

:2876   :ABORD       "42"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "42"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Tananarive";
        :DATE        "1967-07-19"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "07:00";
        :OPERATOR    "Air Madagascar";
        :REGION      "Malagasy Republic";
        :SUMMARY     "Crashed 2,500 feet beyond the runway while taking off from Ivato airport in fog. Lost power to both left engines and struck high ground while trying to return for an emergency landing in poor visibility.";
