        :SUMMARY     "The mail plane explosion in mid-air before crashing to the ground in a snowstorm.";
        :TYPE        "Stinson Model A".

:2514   :ABORD       "298"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "112"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Sioux City";
        :DATE        "1989-07-19"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "16:00";
        :OPERATOR    "United Air Lines";
        :REGION      "Iowa";
        :ROUTE       "Denver, CO - Chicago, IL";
        :SUMMARY     "Catastrophifailure of the No. 2 (rear) engine while en route from Denver to Chicago, with total loss of all three hydraulics systems due to damage.The aircraft maneuvering with only the thrust of the engines, crashed while attempting to land at Sioux City. Failure to detect a fatigue crack in the No. 2 engine resulting in the disintegration of the fan disk and loss of all three hydraulisystems. Subject of the 1992 TV-movie 'Crash Landing: The Rescue of Flight 232.'";
        :TYPE        "McDonnell Douglas DC-10-10".

:3608   :ABORD       "2"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "2"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Columbus";
        :DATE        "2007-12-05"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "06:48";
        :OPERATOR    "Castle Aviation";
        :REGION      "Ohio";
        :ROUTE       "Columbus, OH - Buffalo, NY";
        :SUMMARY     "The cargo plane crashed into a brushy field, inverted, shortly after taking off in heavy snow. Radar data indicated that it was in a left turn at a ground speed of 109 knots before descending and impacting terrain. The plane was carrying checks and other goods for a banking customer. The pilot's failure to maintain aircraft control and collision avoidance with terrain due to spatial disorientation. Contributing to the accident were low cloud ceiling and night conditions.";
        :TYPE        "Cessna 208B Caravan I Super Cargomaster".

:1610   :ABORD       "9"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "6"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Cairo";
        :DATE        "1946-08-24"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :OPERATOR    "Misrair";
        :REGION      "Egypt";
        :SUMMARY     "Crashed and caught fire.";
        :TYPE        "Avro Anson".

:2704   :ABORD       "517"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "1"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Tokyo";
        :DATE        "1999-07-23"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "11:25";
        :OPERATOR    "All Nippon Airways";
        :REGION      "Japan";
        :ROUTE       "Tokyo, Japan - Chitose, Japan";
        :SUMMARY     "Two minutes after taking off from Haneda Airport, a man carrying a knife forced a flight attendant to take him in the cockpit of the plane.  A fan of computer flight-simulation games, he stated he just wanted to fly a real plane.  After forcing the co-pilot out of the cockpit he ordered the captain to fly to a U.S. Air Force base in western Tokyo. When he refused, he stabbed the captain and seized the controls. After a sudden drop in altitude, the co-pilot and an off duty crew member entered the cockpit and overpowered the hijacker.  A one point the plane plunged to within 984 feet of the ground. The plane ultimately  landed safely but the captain died of his injuries.";
        :TYPE        "Boeing B-747".

:1800   :ABORD       "17"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "17"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Jacksonville";
        :DATE        "1955-12-21"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "03:43";
        :OPERATOR    "Eastern Air Lines";
        :REGION      "Florida";
        :ROUTE       "Miami - Jacksonville";
        :SUMMARY     "The plane crashed while on approach and during an attempted go-around.  The crew allowed the aircraft to deviate to the left of course and descent below the glide path for reasons unknown.  The crew encountered local fog and restricted visibility during the final approach of an ILS approach and missed approach procedure came too late to prevent the aircraft from descending into the ground.";
        :TYPE        "Lockheed 749C-79-12 Constellation".

:4391   :ABORD       "11"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "11"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Near Ariab";
        :DATE        "1993-06-07"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :OPERATOR    "Sasco Air Lines";
        :REGION      "Sudan";
        :SUMMARY     "Lost the right engine on takeoff. The pilot returned to the airport and landed with the landing gear retracted. During the slide the left wing struck a rock and ruptured causing the plane to burst into flames.";
        :TYPE        "Cessna 404 Titan".

:4581   :ABORD       "18"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "18"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Near Nakhon Ratchasima ";
        :DATE        "1969-04-25"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "16:00";
        :OPERATOR    "Military - U.S. Air Force";
        :REGION      "Thailand";
        :SUMMARY     "The aircraft crashed shortly after taking off from Korat Air Base. The plane climbed to about 500 ft. and then slammed into the ground and burst into flames. Severe windshear.";
        :TYPE        "Lockheed EC121R".

:4771   :ABORD       "7"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "7"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Cuidad";
        :DATE        "1972-05-08"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :OPERATOR    "Aerotechnia";
        :REGION      "Venezuela";
        :ROUTE       "Ciudad - La Centella";
        :SUMMARY     "Struck a mountain while en route.";
        :TYPE        "Douglas C-47B".

:5022   :ABORD       "6"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "2"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Kinshasa";
        :DATE        "1996-01-08"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "225"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "12:43";
        :OPERATOR    "African Air";
        :REGION      "Zaire";
        :ROUTE       "Kinshasa - Kahemba";
        :SUMMARY     "The aircraft failed to gain altitude after taking off from N'Dolo Airport and ran off the runway and crashed into a market square. The plane was overloaded by 595 lbs. The aircraft certification was revoked and crew did not have authorization to fly. The number killed on the ground varies widely from different sources. The number of fatalities, 225, is derived from the publication Weekly Mail and Guardian in an article covering the court trial of the pilots, charging them with the deaths of 225 people. Some sources quote as many as 350 died.";
        :TYPE        "Antonov AN-32B".

:4961   :ABORD       "2"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "2"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Princeston";
        :DATE        "1966-04-05"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "18:44";
        :OPERATOR    "Layman Weikle - Taxi";
        :REGION      "West Virginia";
        :SUMMARY     "The aircraft crashed after an uncontrolled descent. Carbon Monoxide poisoning from defective exhaust muffler system.";
        :TYPE        "Cessna 172D".

:5212   :ABORD       "15"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "15"^^xsd:int;
        :DATE        "1938-07-29"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "04:11";
        :OPERATOR    "Pan American World Airways";
        :REGION      "PacifiOcean between Manila and Guam";
        :ROUTE       "Alameda - Manila";
        :SUMMARY     "The plane crashed into the ocean while en route between Guam and Manilla. The last known position was 12.27 N, 130.40 W or 582 nm east southeast of Manila at 04:00 GCT. Cause unknown. The plane may have been hijacked by the Japanese and flown to Truk Island where the crew and passengers were murdered. The aircraft was named 'Hawaii Clipper.'";
        :TYPE        "Martin M-130 (flying boat)".

:1008   :ABORD       "7"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "7"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Nova Scotia";
        :DATE        "2004-10-14"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "03:56";
        :OPERATOR    "MK Airlines";
        :REGION      "Canada";
        :ROUTE       "Windsor Locks - Halifax - Zaragoza, Spain";
        :SUMMARY     "The cargo plane did not gain altitude and ran off the end of the runway and crashed into a forest. The aircraft's lower aft fuselage struck a berm supporting a localizer antenna, resulting in the tail separating from the aircraft, rendering the aircraft uncontrollable. The incorrect V speeds and thrust setting were too low to enable the aircraft to take off safely for the actual weight of the aircraft. The pilots of MKA1602 did not carry out the gross error check in accordance with the company's standard operating procedures (SOPs), and the incorrect take-off performance data were not detected. Crew fatigue.";
        :TYPE        "Boeing 747-244B-SF".

:291    :ABORD       "2"^^xsd:int;
