        :SUMMARY     "The aircraft took off from  from Kariba Airport at 17.10.  Shortly after departing Kariba, the starboard wing was hit by a SAM-7 missile.  The crew tried to make an emergency landing in a large clearing in the bush. The aircraft crash landed, striking an irrigation ditch, cart-wheeled, broke up and caught fire.  Soldiers from the Joshua Nkomo's Zimbabwe Peoples Revolution Army, who were responsible for shooting down the airliner, later killed 10 of the 18 survivors. The remaining survivors were rescued the next day.";
        :TYPE        "Vickers Viscount 782D".

:92     :ABORD       "5"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "5"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Aialak Bay";
        :DATE        "1990-06-25"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "14:30";
        :OPERATOR    "Air Taxi - Trail Lake Flying Service Inc.";
        :REGION      "Alaska";
        :ROUTE       "Seward, AK - Aialak Bay, AK";
        :SUMMARY     "Crashed into a 2,700 ft. mountain while on a sightseeing trip.  The pilot-in-command's attempt to fly under visual flight rules while in instrument meteorological conditions. Contributing factors to the accident were the low ceiling and surrounding mountainous terrain.";
        :TYPE        "Cessna 207A".

:189    :ABORD       "8"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "8"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Near Barrow";
        :DATE        "1997-11-08"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "08:08";
        :OPERATOR    "Hageland Aviation Services";
        :REGION      "Alaska";
        :ROUTE       "Barrow - Wainwright";
        :SUMMARY     "A few minutes after takeoff a distress call was received from the aircraft after which it ditched into the sea 200 yards offshore. The pilot's disregard for lateral fuel loading limits, his improper removal of frost prior to takeoff, and the resulting inadvertent stall/spin. Factors involved in this accident were the improper asymmetrical fuel loading which reduced lateral aircraft control, the self-induced pressure to takeoff on time by the pilot, and inadequate surveillance of the company operations by company management.";
        :TYPE        "Cessna 208B Caravan I".

