:3630   :ABORD       "26"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "26"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Urbana";
        :DATE        "1967-03-09"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "11:54";
        :OPERATOR    "Trans World Airlines / Private";
        :REGION      "Ohio";
        :ROUTE       "Pittsburgh - Dayton";
        :SUMMARY     "Midair collision. Twenty five killed on the DC-9, one on the Beechcraft. Failure of the DC-9 crew to see and avoid the Beechcraft. The DC-9 was traveling at almost 300 mph at low altitude in airspace occupied by numerous small planes. The contributing factor to the accident was the excessive speed of the DC-9.  ATC systems inadequate to separate controlled and uncontrolled traffic. After this accident, the FAA imposed a maximum speed of 250 knots below 10,000 ft. mean sea level.";
        :TYPE        "MD Douglas DC-9-15 / Beechcraft Baron-55".

:2486   :ABORD       "102"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "102"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Off Parepare";
        :DATE        "2007-01-01"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "14:07";
        :OPERATOR    "Adam Air";
        :REGION      "Indonesia";
        :ROUTE       "Surabaya, East Java - Manado, Indonesia";
        :SUMMARY     "While flying at FL350 the airliner went missing between Surabaya and Manado in poor weather conditions after the pilot reported strong winds. Wreckage was found 5 miles south of Parepare. The accident was caused by the autopilot being accidentally disconnected. The two pilots had been trying to fix a problem with the plane's navigation instruments when they disconnected the autopilot and lost control of the plane. Without the autopilot, the plane went out of control, listing to the right and pitching down.";
        :TYPE        "Boeing B-737-4Q8".

