        :OPERATOR    "Military - Royal Air Force";
        :REGION      "Canada";
        :ROUTE       "Air Show";
        :SUMMARY     "During a low flying turn manuve, at an air show, the pilot caused the plane to stall and crash into the water. The captain made an error of judgement in modifying one of the display manoeuvres to the extent that he stalled the aircraft at a height and attitude from which recovery was impossible.";
        :TYPE        "British Aerospace Nimrod MR-2P".

:3314   :ABORD       "63"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "29"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Elizabeth";
        :DATE        "1952-02-11"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "4"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "00:20";
        :OPERATOR    "National Airlines";
        :REGION      "New Jersey";
        :SUMMARY     "The aircraft crashed into an apartment complex shortly after taking off. The last message from the pilot was 'I've lost an engine and am returning to field.'   Reversal in flight of No. 3 propeller and subsequent feathering of No. 4 propeller at too low an altitude to effect a recovery.";
        :TYPE        "Douglas DC-6".

:4408   :ABORD       "187"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "176"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Near Paramaribo";
        :DATE        "1989-06-07"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "04:27";
        :OPERATOR    "Surinam Airways";
        :REGION      "Surinam";
        :ROUTE       "Paramaribo - Zanderij";
        :SUMMARY     "The aircraft hit a tree and crashed during a third landing attempt in fog. The crew descended below the published minimum altitude. Despite concerns about possible landing equipment failures the crew was determined to make a landing and not divert to another airport as they were running out of fuel. They could not get an ILS signal and ignored a Ground Proximity Warning System alarm 60 seconds prior to the crash by turning it off 10 seconds after it started its warning. About 20 members from the Dutch soccer team 'Colorful 11' from Surinam were killed.";
        :TYPE        "McDonnell Douglas DC-8 Super 62".

:2410   :ABORD       "1"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "1"^^xsd:int;
