:4997   :ABORD       "73"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "3"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Aden";
        :DATE        "1985-08-15"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :OPERATOR    "Alyemda Airlines";
        :REGION      "Yemen";
        :ROUTE       "Aden - Abu Dahbi";
        :SUMMARY     "As the plane reached FL230, water was spilled on the autopilot panel and the crew had to disengage the autopilot because the stabilizer trim wheel started to rotate. Control was lost as the plane pitched up and down. Control was regained at 1,000 ft. and an emergency landing was carried out.";
        :TYPE        "Boeing 707-336C".

:4065   :ABORD       "145"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "145"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Near Irkutsk";
        :DATE        "2001-07-04"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "02:08";
        :OPERATOR    "Vladivostokavia";
        :REGION      "Russia";
        :ROUTE       "Yekaterinburg - Irkutsk - Vladivostok";
        :SUMMARY     "The plane crashed and exploded in flames in Siberian woodlands near the village of Burdakovka, about 21 miles from Irkutsk. The aircraft crashed during the third turn in a landing approach to Irkutsk, an intermediate stop for refueling. The first officer was flying the plane, when at 2,600 ft., an audible alarm sounded indicating a wide angle of attack. Eleven seconds later the aircraft swung around 180 degrees and entered a flat spin. The captain ordered the engines at full throttle but it was too late and 22 seconds later the plane hit the ground, belly first, broke up and burned. Incorrect actions of the crew. Due to poor communication between pilots, they put in the wrong parameters while landing causing the plane to descend at the wrong angle. As a result, the plane stalled and entered a spin and crashed.";
        :TYPE        "Tupolev TU-154M".

:3161   :ABORD       "65"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "61"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Near Casablanca";
        :DATE        "1958-05-18"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "04:30";
        :OPERATOR    "Sabena";
        :REGION      "Morocco";
        :ROUTE       "Lisbon - Leopoldville";
        :SUMMARY     "The aircraft developed trouble in the No. 1 engine while en route from Lisbon to Leopoldville. While attempting to land in poor visibility on 3 engines, the aircraft stalled 80 ft. above the ground and crashed into a building and burst into flames. Pre-crash damage to the No. 1 engine. An error of judgment by the pilot in reapplication of power when the aircraft was neither in the appropriate configuration nor at a sufficient speed to carry out the attempted safety maneuver.";
        :TYPE        "Douglas DC-7C".

:4255   :ABORD       "19"^^xsd:int;
