        :HOUR        "19:30";
        :OPERATOR    "Junction City Fire Department";
        :REGION      "California";
        :ROUTE       "Ferrying fire fighters";
        :SUMMARY     "The helicopter was ferrying fire fighters in Northern California's Shasta-Trinity National Forest when it crashed. The four survivors were seriously burned, with two listed in critical condition. The helicopter lost main rotor power during liftoff.";
        :TYPE        "Sikorsky S-61N".

:2192   :ABORD       "23"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "19"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Off Oahu";
        :DATE        "1957-12-23"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "16:00";
        :OPERATOR    "Military - U.S. Navy";
        :REGION      "Hawaii";
        :SUMMARY     "The aircraft lost all power during a simulated emergency maneuver and struck the water after descending from a altitude of 1,000 ft. One of the crew moved an emergency shut-off lever in the wrong direction depriving all four engines of their fuel supply. The plane hit the water and broke in two. It was ruled the check pilot had failed to initiate remedial action when the aircraft began to lose altitude and failed to exercise authority when the real emergency developed.";
        :TYPE        "Lockheed WV-2".

