:2701   :ABORD       "133"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "133"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Tokyo Bay";
        :DATE        "1966-02-04"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "19:00";
        :OPERATOR    "All Nippon Airways";
        :REGION      "Japan";
        :ROUTE       "Chitose - Tokyo";
        :SUMMARY     "The jetliner crashed about 7.5 miles ESE of Tokyo International (Haneda) Airport where it was scheduled to land. The aircraft was on VFR approach and was observed at a height of 2, 000 ft. just before the crash.  Cause undetermined. Excessive sink rate is thought to have caused four 727 accidents in succession. Lake Michigan 8/16/65, Cincinnati 11/8/65, Salt Lake City 11/11/65 and Tokyo Bay 2/4/66. Only the Salt Lake and Cincinnati crashes were officially attributed to it. After 727 training manuals were modified and pilots were reoriented to the flying characteristics of the aircraft the problem was corrected.";
        :TYPE        "Boeing B-727-81".

:1557   :ABORD       "55"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "55"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Skagerrak";
        :DATE        "1989-09-08"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "16:36";
        :OPERATOR    "Partnair";
        :REGION      "Denmark";
        :ROUTE       "Oslo - Hamburg";
        :SUMMARY     "The aircraft crashed into the sea after an in-flight breakup. Severe vibration caused by worn bolts causing the rudder to jam and the tail to collapse. Bolts used to attach the fin to the fuselage were found to be counterfeit and wore much faster that genuine bolts.";
        :TYPE        "Convair CV-580".

:1747   :ABORD       "11"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "1"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Sevenoaks";
        :DATE        "1927-08-22"^^xsd:date;
