        :HOUR        "18:20";
        :OPERATOR    "Military - U.S. Navy";
        :REGION      "England";
        :SUMMARY     "Navy lieutenant Joseph P. Kennedy Jr., 29, brother of President John F. Kennedy, was killed while on a flying mission over England during World War II.  Kennedy volunteered for operation Aphrodite after completing two full combat tours and was killed when the explosive-laden PB4Y he was flying blew up in air.  He was intending to aim the ship and bail out, leaving another aircraft to guide the PB4Y via remote control to a German submarine pen on the French coast; it apparently exploded when he armed the switches.  The photographichase plane had President Franklin Roosevelt's son, Elliot Roosevelt, on board.";
        :TYPE        "Consolidated PB4Y-1".

