        :SUMMARY     "The aircraft emerged out of a fog bank while attempting to land, banked to the left and crashed. The pilot's failure to initiate a go-around after emerging from a fog bank on a short final which resulted in inadequate airspeed and a stall. Contributing to the accident was the pilot's poor judgement in attempting the VFR approach in IMC conditions.";
        :TYPE        "Beechcraft C90".

:4744   :ABORD       "91"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "43"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Salt Lake City";
        :DATE        "1965-11-11"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "17:52";
        :OPERATOR    "United Air Lines";
        :REGION      "Utah";
        :ROUTE       "Denver - Salt Lake City";
        :SUMMARY     "The aircraft crashed short of the runway and collided with runway lights, 335 feet short of the runway, causing the main landing gear to fail followed by a fire. Too high of a descent rate during approach. Failure of the captain to take  timely action to arrest an excessive descent rate during the landing approach. Excessive sink rate is thought to have caused four 727 accidents in succession. Lake Michigan 8/16/65, Cincinnati 11/8/65, Salt Lake City 11/11/65 and Tokyo Bay 2/4/66. Only the Salt Lake and Cincinnati crashes were officially attributed to it. After 727 training manuals were modified and pilots were reoriented to the flying characteristics of the aircraft the problem was corrected. Bill Linderman, 45, champion rodeo cowboy killled.";
        :TYPE        "Boeing B-727-22".

:3840   :ABORD       "30"^^xsd:int;
        :CASUALTIES  "4"^^xsd:int;
        :CITY        "Jolo";
        :DATE        "1982-07-11"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :OPERATOR    "Philippine Air Lines";
        :REGION      "Philippines";
        :SUMMARY     "Takeoff was aborted at V1 when the crew heard unusual sounds from the No.1 engine. The aircraft overran the runway and came to rest against a wall and some vehicles. Misjudged speed and distance and delayed action in aborting the takeoff.";
        :TYPE        "Hawker Siddeley HS-748-209 Srs. 2".

