        :DATE        "1998-09-14"^^xsd:date;
        :GROUND      "0"^^xsd:int;
        :HOUR        "11:52";
        :OPERATOR    "Air taxi - Air Safaris Inc.";
        :REGION      "New Zealand";
        :ROUTE       "Sightseeing";
        :SUMMARY     "The aircraft hit the face of  mountain. The aircraft probably encountered a strong laminar downdraught before entering a thin cloud layer before impact. Although ample escape options were available to the pilot to turn away from the rising terrain and cloud ahead, he did not make a timely decision to do so. Why the pilot did not make a timely turn away could not be explained.";
        :TYPE        "Cessna 177B Cardinal".

